# Fresh VPS Provisioning Guide: AI DebugScan v3

This guide provides step-by-step instructions to set up a clean Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 server for the AI DebugScan platform.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This assumes you have just reinstalled Ubuntu and have a fresh terminal as `root`.

## 1. System Preparation
Update the system and install essential tools.
```bash
apt update && apt upgrade -y
apt install -y curl git unzip build-essential software-properties-common
```

## 2. Install PHP 8.2 & Extensions
The application requires PHP 8.2 and specific libraries for PostgreSQL, XML, and Zip support.
```bash
add-apt-repository ppa:ondrej/php -y
apt update
apt install -y php8.2-fpm php8.2-cli php8.2-pgsql php8.2-xml php8.2-mbstring php8.2-zip php8.2-curl php8.2-intl
```

## 3. Install Web & Database Servers
```bash
apt install -y nginx postgresql postgresql-contrib
```

### Configure PostgreSQL
Create the database and a dedicated user.
```bash
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE DATABASE aidebugscan;"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE USER scanuser WITH PASSWORD 'SET_YOUR_PASSWORD_HERE';"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE aidebugscan TO scanuser;"
```

## 4. Install Composer
```bash
curl -sS https://getcomposer.org/installer | php
mv composer.phar /usr/local/bin/composer
```

## 5. Set Up Git-Based Deployment
This allows you to deploy by simply running `git push production main`.

### Create the Repositories
```bash
mkdir -p /var/repo/ai-debugscan3.git
cd /var/repo/ai-debugscan3.git
git init --bare
```

### Create the Post-Receive Hook
Create a file at `/var/repo/ai-debugscan3.git/hooks/post-receive`:
```bash
nano /var/repo/ai-debugscan3.git/hooks/post-receive
```

**Paste the following content**:
```bash
#!/bin/bash
TARGET="/var/www/ai-debugscan3"
GIT_DIR="/var/repo/ai-debugscan3.git"

mkdir -p $TARGET
git --work-tree=$TARGET --git-dir=$GIT_DIR checkout -f main

# Set permissions
chown -R www-data:www-data $TARGET

# Run Composer automatically
cd $TARGET
sudo -u www-data composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader
```
**Make it executable**:
```bash
chmod +x /var/repo/ai-repo/ai-debugscan3.git/hooks/post-receive
```

## 6. Nginx Configuration
Create a site file at `/etc/nginx/sites-available/aidebugscan`:
```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name YOUR_IP_OR_DOMAIN;
    root /var/www/ai-debugscan3/public;

    index index.php;

    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.php?$query_string;
    }

    location ~ \.php$ {
        include snippets/fastcgi-php.conf;
        fastcgi_pass unix:/var/run/php/php8.2-fpm.sock;
    }
}
```
**Enable and restart**:
```bash
ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/aidebugscan /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
rm /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default
systemctl restart nginx
```

## 7. Background Worker (Systemd)
Create `/etc/systemd/system/scan-worker.service`:
```ini
[Unit]
Description=AI DebugScan Background Worker
After=network.target postgresql.service

[Service]
Type=simple
User=www-data
WorkingDirectory=/var/www/ai-debugscan3
ExecStart=/usr/bin/php /var/www/ai-debugscan3/workers/scan_worker.php
Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```
**Start the worker**:
```bash
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl enable --now scan-worker
```

## 8. Final Local Steps (on your computer)
Update your local Git remote to point to the new server:
```powershell
git remote remove production
git remote add production root@YOUR_IP_ADDRESS:/var/repo/ai-debugscan3.git
git push production main --force
```
